				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12892535/elliot-edna-had-a-son-named-tim#post-4496171</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 10 Feb 2020 18:55:22 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>MaliceAforethought</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2902864</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>This is remarkably compelling for a tale where, essentially, nothing much of anything happens. I'm excited to read what it's setting the scene for: the characters feel well-rounded and real, and the world feels incredibly real as well &#8212; probably, now I come to think of it, because nothing even vaguely anomalous happens throughout. It's <em>our</em> world, but it plays that to its strength and ends up with a delightfully nostalgic vignette where nobody dies, no laws of physics are violated, and the Foundation doesn't get so much as a name-check.</p> <p>Which, for a tale on this site, is an abnormality. But it's a testament to your skills that I didn't notice until writing this.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
